    LLM: "Identify your partner! In a Normal Game, watch who plays the black Queens. If you don't have one, your partner is the other person who doesn't play one.\n\nThe 'Ten' Flush: Since Tens are worth 10 points and are high trumps, use your top three trumps (â™¥A, â™£10, â™ 10) to 'flush' the remaining Tens out of the opponents' hands as early as possible.\n\nZolo Du (Solo Tout) Detection: If you see someone bid Solo Tout, they almost certainly hold the top three trumps. Your only hope is to hold the 4th top trump (â™¥10) and wait to trap their lead.",
